---
import TreatmentPage from "../../../components/TreatmentPage.astro";

const T = "/services/fertility-treatment";
const A = "/services/assessment";

const page = {
  slug: "male-fertility-test",
  name: "Male Fertility Testing",
  title: "Male Fertility Test and Sperm Testing | Kamran Fertility Clinic",
  description: "Discuss a male fertility test with Dr. Kamran Saleem. Review semen reports, hormone tests and history to decide which investigations may be appropriate.",
  eyebrow: "Male Fertility Testing",
  h1: "Male Fertility Testing and Test Planning",
  waText: "Hello, I would like to book a male fertility testing assessment with Dr. Kamran Saleem.",
  ctaLabel: "Book an assessment",
  heroSub: [
    "Male fertility testing can help investigate sperm-related factors when conception is delayed or a concern has been identified.",
    "The assessment helps determine which tests are relevant and how results should be reviewed.",
  ].join(" "),
  leadIn: [
    { rich: ["This assessment is part of a wider fertility evaluation. The tests selected depend on your history, symptoms and previous results. Explore the related ", ["Fertility Assessment & Diagnosis", A], " pathway, or read the educational guide ", ["Male Fertility Test: What to Know", "/resources/male-fertility-test"], "."] },
  ],
  sections: [
    {
      id: "male-fertility-test-purpose",
      title: "What Is Included in Male Fertility Testing?",
      intro: "Testing is selected to investigate possible factors affecting sperm and reproductive health.",
      icon: "flask",
      body: [
        "A semen analysis is commonly an initial laboratory test. Depending on the findings and history, a clinician may discuss additional assessment or selected blood tests.",
        { ul: [
          "Review of previous fertility and medical history",
          "Semen analysis when appropriate",
          "Hormone testing if symptoms or results suggest it",
          "Physical examination where the clinician considers it relevant",
          "Follow-up to explain findings and possible next steps",
        ] },
        { rich: ["For details on the sample and report, see our dedicated ", ["semen analysis", `${A}/semen-analysis`], " page."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "when-male-testing",
      title: "When Testing May Be Recommended",
      intro: "Testing may be considered as part of a couple’s fertility evaluation or for a specific male reproductive concern.",
      icon: "calendar",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "Difficulty conceiving after 12 months of trying, or sooner when a partner is 35 or older",
          "A previous semen report outside the laboratory reference range",
          "A history that may affect testicular or reproductive function",
          "Symptoms or examination findings that need assessment",
          "Being assessed alongside a partner’s fertility evaluation",
        ] },
        "Male factors contribute to a significant share of couples’ fertility problems, which is why testing is usually recommended early rather than only after the female partner has been fully investigated.",
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "tests-that-may-be-considered",
      title: "Tests That May Be Considered",
      intro: "The tests depend on what the history and the first results show.",
      icon: "compare",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "Semen analysis: volume, sperm concentration, motility and morphology",
          "Repeat semen analysis, since results can vary between samples",
          "Blood hormone tests such as testosterone, FSH and LH in selected cases",
          "Further investigations if no sperm are found or the history suggests a specific cause",
        ] },
        { rich: ["See ", ["hormonal analysis", `${A}/hormonal-analysis`], " for how hormone tests are chosen and reviewed."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "preparing-male-test",
      title: "Before Your Appointment",
      intro: "Follow the laboratory instructions for any test you are scheduled to have.",
      icon: "clipboard",
      body: [
        "If a semen sample is requested, confirm the collection method and abstinence instructions with the laboratory. Abstinence advice is often given as a short range of days, but requirements can vary. Tell the clinician about medicines, supplements, recent illness or fever, and previous test results.",
        { rich: ["For detailed interpretation, read ", ["Understanding a Semen Analysis", "/resources/understanding-a-semen-analysis"], "."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "male-test-results",
      title: "Understanding the Results",
      intro: "A single result may not provide the complete picture.",
      icon: "compare",
      body: [
        "Results are interpreted alongside the medical history and, when needed, repeat testing or further investigations. The clinician can explain what a finding may mean and whether it changes the next step.",
        { rich: ["If more detailed evaluation is needed, see ", ["male infertility assessment", `${A}/male-infertility`], " or ", ["hormonal analysis", `${A}/hormonal-analysis`], "."] },
      ],
    },
    {
      id: "improving-sperm-health",
      title: "Lifestyle and Sperm Health",
      intro: "Some everyday factors may be worth discussing with the clinician.",
      icon: "route",
      body: [
        { ul: [
          "Smoking, heavy alcohol use and recreational drugs can affect semen quality",
          "Prolonged heat exposure to the testes may be relevant for some men",
          "Certain medicines and supplements, including anabolic steroids, can affect sperm production",
          "Weight, sleep and general health are also worth reviewing",
        ] },
        "Sperm take around three months to develop, so changes may take time to show up in a repeat test. A clinician can advise on what is realistic for your situation.",
        { rich: ["If treatment becomes relevant, you can read about our ", ["fertility treatment", T], " services. For a partner’s evaluation, see ", ["female fertility assessment", `${A}/female-fertility-test`], "."] },
      ],
    },
  ],
  faqs: [
    { q: "Is male fertility testing only a semen analysis?", a: "Semen analysis is commonly an initial test, but other investigations may be considered when the history or results indicate them." },
    { q: "Can I bring a previous semen report?", a: "Yes. Bring the complete report, including the laboratory name and date, if available." },
    { q: "Will I need more than one test?", a: "Sometimes. The clinician or laboratory may recommend repeat or additional testing depending on the initial findings." },
    { q: "When should a man get a fertility test?", a: "Commonly after 12 months of trying without conception, or earlier when there is a known concern, a previous abnormal result or a partner who is 35 or older." },
    { q: "Can lifestyle changes improve male fertility?", a: "In some cases they may help. Stopping smoking, reducing alcohol and reviewing medicines are common topics, but results vary and a clinician can advise individually." },
    { q: "Is the test confidential?", a: "Consultations are private. You can ask the clinic how your reports and information will be handled before the appointment." },
  ],
  closingHeading: "Male Fertility Testing with Dr. Kamran Saleem",
  closingParas: [
    "Dr. Kamran Saleem can review your history and available reports, discuss whether this assessment is appropriate, and explain possible next steps. The exact tests and plan depend on your individual circumstances.",
    "You can ask about the consultation and any separate test fees before confirming an appointment.",
  ],
  resources: [
    { href: "/resources/male-fertility-test", category: "Fertility Assessment", title: "Male Fertility Test: What to Know" },
    { href: "/resources/understanding-a-semen-analysis", category: "Fertility Assessment", title: "Understanding a Semen Analysis" },
    { href: "/resources/male--infertility-consultation", category: "Fertility Assessment", title: "Male Infertility Consultation" },
  ],
  close: {
    heading: "Need Help Choosing the Right Assessment?",
    body: "Share your symptoms, history or previous reports when booking so the consultation can focus on your questions.",
    cta: "Book an assessment",
  },
};
---

<TreatmentPage {...page} />
